# Static-analysis findings triaged as false positives (or as what the
# tool cannot see past). static-analysis.sh fails on any finding not
# listed here, and on any entry listed without a reason.
# One line per finding (repeated when reported more than once), without
# line numbers: tool<TAB>severity<TAB>file<TAB>check<TAB>message
# A "## <reason>" line documents the entries below it.
# Regenerate with: tests/hardening/static-analysis.sh <build> --update-baseline
# (reasons are kept for findings that are still reported).

## Flagged inside libstdc++'s std::string move constructor, reached from std::operator+; no pointer of ours is NULL there.
gcc -fanalyzer -O0	warning	Src/Settings.cpp	-Wanalyzer-null-argument	use of NULL where non-null expected [CWE-476]

## Reported at the fopen() itself, the point where the analysis of that path stopped at its budget: the FILE is closed on every return (fclose() in createManualTimeZone, the FilePtr unique_ptr in parseTimeZone).
